From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:30:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Do not read the destination world while copying a villager

When a villager goes through a portal, Folia builds the copy for the
destination world on the source world's region thread. Creating and
restoring the brain updates the schedule activity, which reads the
destination world state and throws "World mismatch", so the villager is
lost.

Skip that initial update while the current region belongs to another
world. The core UpdateActivityFromSchedule behaviour sets the activity on
the villager's first tick in the new world.

Fixes PaperMC/Folia#431
Related to PaperMC/Folia#446 (nekoneko2872)

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/npc/villager/Villager.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/npc/villager/Villager.java
index 086334694874fccaf7aad9d6d1dde78cfd961c3c..c9505300a4c7c42ef99713863e9301a9a47f16b3 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/npc/villager/Villager.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/npc/villager/Villager.java
@@ -213,7 +213,13 @@ public class Villager extends AbstractVillager implements VillagerDataHolder, Re
             brain.setSchedule(EnvironmentAttributes.VILLAGER_ACTIVITY);
         }
 
-        brain.updateActivityFromSchedule(this.level().environmentAttributes(), this.level().getLevelData().getGameTime(), this.position()); // Folia - region threading - not in the world yet
+        // Tessera start - during an async portal teleport the copy is built on the source world's region, so reading the
+        // destination's environment throws "World mismatch"; the core UpdateActivityFromSchedule behaviour sets it on the next tick
+        final io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.RegionizedWorldData currentWorldData = io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.TickRegionScheduler.getCurrentRegionizedWorldData();
+        if (currentWorldData == null || currentWorldData.world == this.level()) {
+            brain.updateActivityFromSchedule(this.level().environmentAttributes(), this.level().getLevelData().getGameTime(), this.position()); // Folia - region threading - not in the world yet
+        }
+        // Tessera end
     }
 
     @Override
